ground_truth.body:
Logic/order issue: this call to `VULKAN_INTERNAL_TextureTransitionToDefaultUsage(...)` happens *before* checking `if (!texture) return;`, so on allocation failure you will dereference `texture` (NULL) inside the transition function. Move the NULL check immediately after `CreateTexture` and only transition when non-NULL.

```suggestion
    texture = VULKAN_INTERNAL_CreateTexture(
        renderer,
        false,
        &container->header.info);

    if (!texture) {
        return;
    }

    VULKAN_INTERNAL_TextureTransitionToDefaultUsage(
        renderer,
        commandBuffer,
        VULKAN_TEXTURE_USAGE_MODE_UNINITIALIZED,
        texture);
```

